    # large-batch kernel. That structure's per-lane integer div/mod, the two
    # component selects, the vector-base subtraction and the gather-address
    # computation all run on the scalar pipe, which the profiler shows is the
    # bottleneck (~69%) for the small dim-last workloads. The stride-3 loads
    # hit L2 and issue to the (under-utilized ~30%) vector pipe, so this trades
    # scalar-pipe index work for cheap L2 traffic on small inputs.
